/Alt (The four-panel diagram presents spatial distributions of initial conditions and data for a traffic simulation. Panel A displays the initial car density distribution, which decreases from high values in the suburbs to nearly zero in the city center. Panel B shows the urban porosity, with the highest building density at the city center and more open space for traffic flow in the suburbs. Panel C depicts the initial desired velocity field, which points toward the city center and decreases as vehicle density grows. Panel D presents the wind field, with a constant reference wind blowing from the northwest and a noticeably lower velocity inside the city due to the urban porosity distribution.)
